e-Return Intermediaries API Specifications ERI List External Agency Central & State Government Department/Approved Undertaking Agency RBI Approved Banks Tax Deductor & Collector Registration Service Available Downloads Help Do not have an account? Register Already have an account? Login test Search Home Home 1. Form 3 under the “Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme” is now available for online filing 2. Due dates for filing of Income Tax Returns and Audit Reports for AY 2026-27 are extended in the cases of persons mentioned at Sl.No.2 in the Table below Explanation2 to Sub-section (1) of Section 139 of Income Tax Act 1961 vide Circular No.07/2026 dated 28th September,2026. 3. Form 1 under the “Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme” is now available for filing. 4. ITR-1, ITR-2, ITR-3, ITR-4, ITR-5, ITR-6 and ITR-7 for AY 2026-27 are available for filing through both online and offline utilities. 5. Filing of TDS/TCS Correction Statements pertaining to Tax Year 2026-27 has been enabled. 6. Demand Management Facilitation Centre (DFC), has been set up to guide Taxpayers on issues/grievances regarding their outstanding demands. DFC may be contacted through the e-mail id: taxdemand@cpc.incometax.gov.in or on the toll-free number - 1800 309 0131 or chargeable no. 0821-6671200. 7. Excel utilities for filing Updated return for ITR-1 to 7 for AY 2022-23 as per Finance Act, 2026 are available for filing ! ❚❚ Previous Next What's New Stay updated with the latest announcements Rollout of Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme (FADS), 2026 on the Income Tax Portal The Income Tax Department has enabled the Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme, 2026 (FADS 2026) on the e-Filing Portal. Introduced as a one-time compliance opportunity by the Government, this scheme allows eligible taxpayers to voluntarily disclose specified foreign assets and foreign income that were not reported. Under the scheme, eligible taxpayers can furnish the prescribed declaration form online through the e-Filing Portal. Navigation Path: e-File → Income Tax Forms → File Income Tax Forms → Under Other Acts → Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme, 2026 (Form 1 of FADS 2026) For detailed information and filing guidance, please refer to the FADS 2026 Documentation and User Guide available on the Income Tax Portal. Take this opportunity to regularize previously undisclosed foreign assets and income through the Government's one-time voluntary disclosure scheme. New Integrated Payment Module Goes Live on e‑Filing Portal Seamless payments now enabled across both the Income‑tax Act, 1961 and the Income‑tax Act, 2025. With this enhancement, taxpayers can conveniently make payments under the existing Income‑tax Act, 1961 for dues up to FY 2025‑26, as well as under the Income‑tax Act, 2025 for Tax Year 2026‑27 onwards—all from a single interface. Quick Links Access all services at your fingertips NUDGE Campaign e-Pay Tax e-Verify Return Instant E-PAN Tax Calendar Income Tax Calculator Know Tax Payment Status Link Aadhaar/View Status Comply to Notice Authenticate notice/order issued by ITD Verify PAN Status Verify Service Request Know Your JAO Know TAN Details Download CSI File Report Account Misuse Submit Information on Tax Evasion or Benami Property Tax Information & Services Latest Updates Stay ahead with real-time notifications and critical announcements 27 Oct 2026 News Circular CBDT has proposed the Income-tax (Seventh Amendment) Rules, 2026, introducing Rule 281A and new Form 173A for furnishing information to claim exemption on interest income and capital gains from Government securities under Schedule IV of the Income-tax Act, 2025. Click here Read more 12 Oct 2026 News Circular CBDT Notification No. 133/2026 amends the 1988 notification to specify that Joint Commissioners (Appeals) and Additional Commissioners (Appeals) shall be subordinate to the jurisdictional Principal Chief Commissioner or Chief Comm