      "excerpt": "Bonjour ! - Lawless French - Online French Learning French lessons and language tools from Laura K Lawless Chatbot Cool Tools Pronommeur Subjunctivisor Verb Deconjugator Verb Tables Daily Practice FAQ French 101 P w LF Search Welcome! About LKL Beyond Lawless French French Essentials French for Beginners Frequently Asked Questions Independent Study Lessons by Level Log in Online Learning Tips Relearning French Sitemap Subscribe to Lawless French Support LF Teachers’ Tips and Tools The Fine Print",
      "text_length": 4787,
      "checked_at": "2026-10-28T08:43:59+00:00",
      "text": "Bonjour ! - Lawless French - Online French Learning French lessons and language tools from Laura K Lawless Chatbot Cool Tools Pronommeur Subjunctivisor Verb Deconjugator Verb Tables Daily Practice FAQ French 101 P w LF Search Welcome! About LKL Beyond Lawless French French Essentials French for Beginners Frequently Asked Questions Independent Study Lessons by Level Log in Online Learning Tips Relearning French Sitemap Subscribe to Lawless French Support LF Teachers’ Tips and Tools The Fine Print Ad and Affiliate Disclosure Privacy Policy What’s New Workbook ✏️ Bonjour ! et bienvenue à Lawless French , a free resource for students, teachers, and lovers of the beautiful French language. New here? Take a look at my Welcome Page , or just scroll to start exploring some of the most popular features on the site. If you’re a regular visitor, click to discover what’s new . À bientôt ! Lessons by Level Lessons and exercises ranked according to six levels of language proficiency. French 101 Self-study course with lessons, cultural tips, listening exercises, and quizzes. Daily Practice Ideas Regular practice is key – just 15 minutes a day can make all the difference. Grammar Parts of speech, sentence structure, conjugations, and all the other rules. Pronunciation Letters, letter combinations, liaisons, accents, contractions, and more. Vocabulary Themed vocab lists + wordy lessons: synonyms, prefixes, abbreviations… Quizzes and Tests Assorted quizzes, online proficiency test, and info about official certification. The Subjunctivisor! Does [ insert verb | expression | conjunction ] require the subjunctive? Verb Tables 1,600+ French verbs conjugated into all the simple tenses and moods. Langua French Chat Practice speaking French any time of day or night with a human-like AI. Progress with Lawless French Find your level to get a personalized study plan and learning resources. Frantastique Story-based learning with daily lessons, dialogues, historical notes, and comics. French Language Skills Reading Listening Speaking Writing French proficiency test by Stay up to date with Lawless French Questions about French? Visit the Progress with Lawless French Q+A forum to get help from native French speakers and fellow learners. Support Lawless French This free website is created with love and a great deal of work. If you love it, please consider making a one-time or monthly donation . What’s New at Lawless French? Dents du bonheur - Dents de la chance If you have a gap between your front teeth, you’re in luck! Read about the idiomatic French expressions dents du bonheur and dents de la chance . Discussion - Object Pronouns Quiz Test yourself on direct object pronouns and indirect object pronouns with this fill-in-the-blanks exercise: La discussion Note: You must be logged into your Progress with Lawless French account to take this test. If you don’t have one, sign up – it’s free! Relearning French Is your French as rusty as an old can? Did you live in France years ago or study it in high school—and promptly forget everything upon leaving? The fact is that language ability fades with lack of practice. If you used to know French but haven’t spoken it in years or decades, the bad news is that it probably won’t come rushing back all at once. But the good news is that you can relearn it much more quickly than if you were starting out without that previous knowledge. Prendre - to take The irregular French verb prendre literally means “to take,” but also has a number of additional meanings and is used in many idiomatic expressions. Demonstrations and Strikes For better or for worse, demonstrations and strikes are an important part of French society. Here’s some vocabulary to help you understand the news as well as links to further information. Pas de souci Want to learn how to use the French expression pas de souci ? No problem! Free newsletter Please leave this field empty Lawless French is sent every Tuesday and Friday with the latest lessons and features. Email * Please check your email and click the link to confirm your subscription - merci ! © 2026 Lawless French. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Created by Laura K Lawless , author of French Workbook for Dummies and French Essentials for Dummies Hosted by PeoplesHost Cassie by ThemeMeme Subscribe to the free Lawless French newsletter Get new lessons and features in your inbox 2x per week Grammar, vocab, pronunciation lessons Expression of the week Quizzes and exercises Listening and reading comprehension Cultural content Occasional product reviews + offers Subscribe Bonjour ! Lawless French is a free website . Please disable your ad-blocker or donate to support my work . BONUS Donate US$5 / month to unlock le Mot du jour . I'll make a donation I'll disable my ad-blocker",
